{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05XJ", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-smooth-surjective-morphism-implies-algebraic}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{theorem-bootstrap}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a303cf3e472e7e58fe5268695dec322789a0f072660cf6b6592e30e814c34475", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma is the analogue of\nAlgebraic Stacks, Lemma\n<REF_0001>\nand will be superseded by the stronger\nTheorem <REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f9d554b1f008814a4f0e165c77fbc28aa5460911f772658d32e9148c9cd7d54a", "unit_id": "tag:05XJ:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05XJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$u : \\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$1$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0006": "$u$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Delta : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times \\mathcal{X}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-flat-finite-presentation-surjective-diagonal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:745cf17c9fe98b52ecff7fa969684eaf1d5209538a04e38975359affc99dfdaa", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e147ddd31873be4f131ad8f79e449341db7238a6664eeba880e6c7cd7e88464c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a <MATH_0003>-morphism of\nstacks in groupoids over <MATH_0004>. If\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0005> is representable by an algebraic space, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0006> is representable by algebraic spaces, surjective, flat and\nlocally of finite presentation,\n<STRUCT_0004>\nthen\n<MATH_0007>\nrepresentable by algebraic spaces.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7fc5c55ab026b6130e6aa9b0722cec7099ca6afda7346e16c0c9da02743114d2", "unit_id": "tag:05XW:statement"}
{"chapter": "criteria", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05XJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T_1$", "MATH_0002": "$T_2$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{T}_i = (\\Sch/T_i)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$1$", "MATH_0006": "$f_i : \\mathcal{T}_i \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$2$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{T}_1 \\times_\\mathcal{X} \\mathcal{T}_2$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{T}_1 \\times_\\mathcal{X} \\mathcal{T}_2$", "MATH_0010": "$F$", "MATH_0011": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0012": "$U$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0014": "$$\n\\mathcal{T}_i' = \\mathcal{U} \\times_{u, \\mathcal{X}, f_i} \\mathcal{T}_i\n$$", "MATH_0015": "$T'_i$", "MATH_0016": "$S$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{T}_1' \\times_\\mathcal{U} \\mathcal{T}_2'$", "MATH_0018": "$T'_1 \\times_U T'_2$", "MATH_0019": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n&\n\\mathcal{T}_1 \\times_{\\mathcal X} \\mathcal{T}_2 \\ar[rr]\\ar'[d][dd] & &\n\\mathcal{T}_1 \\ar[dd] \\\\\n\\mathcal{T}_1' \\times_\\mathcal{U} \\mathcal{T}_2' \\ar[ur]\\ar[rr]\\ar[dd] & &\n\\mathcal{T}_1' \\ar[ur]\\ar[dd] \\\\\n&\n\\mathcal{T}_2 \\ar'[r][rr] & &\n\\mathcal X \\\\\n\\mathcal{T}_2' \\ar[rr]\\ar[ur] & &\n\\mathcal{U} \\ar[ur] }\n$$", "MATH_0020": "$2$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{T}_1' \\times_\\mathcal{U} \\mathcal{T}_2' \\to\n\\mathcal{T}_1 \\times_{\\mathcal X} \\mathcal{T}_2$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0023": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{T}_1' \\times_\\mathcal{U} \\mathcal{T}_2' \\ar[d] \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{U} \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathcal{T}_1 \\times_{\\mathcal X} \\mathcal{T}_2 \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{X}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0024": "$2$", "MATH_0025": "$T'_1 \\times_U T'_2 \\to F$", "MATH_0026": "$F$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-representable-diagonal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{stacks-lemma-2-fibre-product-stacks-in-setoids-over-stack-in-groupoids}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{stacks-lemma-stack-in-setoids-characterize}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-map-fibred-setoids-representable-algebraic-spaces}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-base-change-representable-by-spaces}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-map-fibred-setoids-property}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{algebraic-lemma-base-change-representable-transformations-property}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{bootstrap-theorem-final-bootstrap}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:78094db3028e231759bb22976e3ac5a792c1f82156f8757e5000bf4a7ed506c7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:db83847bb967d995588515a233ff2bfbe8cf839ee2f8b821b2234e5f5c3f72eb", "source_text": "Given two schemes <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> over <MATH_0003> denote\n<MATH_0004> the associated representable\nfibre categories. Suppose given <MATH_0005>-morphisms\n<MATH_0006>.\nAccording to\nAlgebraic Stacks, Lemma <REF_0001>\nit suffices to prove that the <MATH_0007>-fibered\nproduct <MATH_0008>\nis representable by an algebraic space. By\nStacks, Lemma\n<REF_0002>\nthis is in any case a stack in setoids. Thus\n<MATH_0009> corresponds\nto some sheaf <MATH_0010> on <MATH_0011>, see\nStacks, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0012> be the algebraic space which represents <MATH_0013>.\nBy assumption\n<MATH_0014>\nis representable by an algebraic space <MATH_0015> over <MATH_0016>. Hence\n<MATH_0017> is representable\nby the algebraic space <MATH_0018>.\nConsider the commutative diagram\n<MATH_0019>\nIn this diagram the bottom square, the right square, the back square, and\nthe front square are <MATH_0020>-fibre products. A formal argument then shows\nthat <MATH_0021>\nis the ``base change'' of <MATH_0022>, more precisely\nthe diagram\n<MATH_0023>\nis a <MATH_0024>-fibre square.\nHence <MATH_0025> is representable by algebraic spaces,\nflat, locally of finite presentation and surjective, see\nAlgebraic Stacks, Lemmas\n<REF_0004>,\n<REF_0005>,\n<REF_0006>, and\n<REF_0007>.\nTherefore <MATH_0026> is an algebraic space by\nBootstrap, Theorem <REF_0008>\nand we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a21e63bdde256423d353824bd51609d3e073c6f93381235bcd6dacf1c6272c42", "unit_id": "tag:05XW:proof"}
